    {
      "id": "m70",
      "at": "2026-11-24T12:31:00Z",
      "role": "emil",
      "text": "why did search latency jump on Friday? no need for a track, just tell me"
    },
    {
      "id": "m71",
      "at": "2026-11-24T12:34:00Z",
      "role": "desk",
      "steps": 9,
      "text": "The jump is the new ranking step, not the index.\n\n- p95 of `/search` went from 84 ms to 131 ms with Friday's 16:10 deploy, which turned on re-ranking for every query.\n- The index build and the cache hit rate are unchanged across the deploy.\n- Re-ranking only pays off for queries of three words or more, about a fifth of traffic.\n\nLimiting re-ranking to those queries should bring p95 back near 90 ms. search-latency is already measuring with `make bench`, so I would let it try that next."
    },
    {
      "id": "m72",
      "at": "2026-11-24T12:41:00Z",
      "role": "report",
      "session": "b25e44d1-7c8d-4e9f-8a1b-2c3d4e5f6a72",
      "outcome": "done",
      "text": "bun replaces node in the Dockerfile and CI, and bun test passes. Branch bun/queue-api."
